                    "content": "### Description\n373 views\nPosted: 2026-09-28\nThe early exuberance of AI adoption has run up against hard-nosed business requirements around managing costs, protecting sensitive data, and matching the right model with the right job at the right price.\nOn today’s show, sponsor Broadcom is here to make a case that private cloud is the place for AI inferencing workloads. We talk about the new VMware AI Factory that combines software and hardware to accelerate deployment and operations, curated models that make it easy to deliver inferencing “as a service” to internal customers, and more.\nMy guest is Sabina Anja, Chief Technologist | Executive Advisor - VMware Cloud Foundation. [...] ### Transcript\n[0:04] Welcome to Tech Bites. So, the early exuberance of AI adoption is now running up against hard-nosed business requirements around things like managing costs, protecting sensitive data, and\n[0:13] matching the right model with the right job at the right price. On today's show, sponsor Broadc",
